      "problem": "Calculate \n${\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})) \\\\  & =-1-(-\\sqrt{2}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
